# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivenix Partners — Environment Variables Reference
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env to version control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get this from https://console.neon.tech → your project → Connection string
# Use the "pooled" connection string for the API server.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ── Session ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# ── First Admin Bootstrap (one-time setup) ──────────────────────────────────
# Set these to create the initial admin account. After first login, change the
# password and unset/remove these variables.
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=admin@trivinexpartners.com
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-secure-password

# ── CORS (production API server only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins.
# Example: https://yourapp.vercel.app,https://yourdomain.com
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourapp.vercel.app,https://yourdomain.com

# ── Email / SMTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use Gmail SMTP with a Google App Password (not your normal Gmail password).
# Enable 2-Step Verification on the Google account, then generate an App Password.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-company@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-gmail-app-password
SMTP_FROM="Trivenix Partners <your-company@gmail.com>"
ADMIN_EMAIL=your-company@gmail.com

# ── AI Assistant (Google Gemini) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. Never expose in VITE_ variables or the browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash

# ── Media Storage (Cloudinary) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. If not configured, admins can still add YouTube/Vimeo/external
# video URLs as a fallback. File uploads will be unavailable.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloudinary-cloud-name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your-cloudinary-api-key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your-cloudinary-api-secret

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deployment Quick-Start
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. DATABASE — Neon (https://neon.tech)
#    - Create a free project
#    - Copy the "pooled" connection string → DATABASE_URL
#    - Run schema: pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push
#    - Seed: pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server exec tsx src/scripts/seed.ts
#
# 2. API SERVER — Railway (https://railway.app)
#    - New project → Deploy from GitHub repo
#    - Set root directory: (leave as root — railway.toml handles build)
#    - Add all env vars from this file (DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, etc.)
#    - Copy the Railway public URL → use in ALLOWED_ORIGINS + vercel.json rewrite
#
# 3. FRONTEND — Vercel (https://vercel.com)
#    - Import GitHub repo
#    - Set root directory to: artifacts/craftloop
#    - Framework preset: Vite
#    - Build command: cd ../.. && pnpm install && pnpm --filter @workspace/craftloop run build
#    - Output dir: dist/public
#    - No VITE_ secrets needed (admin auth is cookie-based)
#    - In vercel.json, replace REPLACE_WITH_RAILWAY_API_URL with your Railway URL
#
# 4. Gmail SMTP Setup
#    - Enable Google 2-Step Verification on the sender account
#    - Generate an App Password (16 characters)
#    - Set SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASS in Railway env vars
#    - Restart/redeploy the API
#    - Use the admin "Email Integration → Send Test Email" to verify
#
# 5. Gemini API Setup
#    - Get an API key from https://aistudio.google.com
#    - Set GEMINI_API_KEY and GEMINI_MODEL in Railway env vars
#    - Redeploy the API
#
# 6. Cloudinary Setup (optional, for file uploads)
#    - Create a free account at https://cloudinary.com
#    - Set CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
#    - Without these, admins can still use YouTube/Vimeo/external video URLs
#
# 7. Verify the production domain, forms, admin, email, AI and media.
